      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "1. **Identify the Perimeter of the Given Triangle:**\n\n   Given the side lengths of the triangle as 6 cm, 7 cm, and 9 cm, we can calculate the perimeter by summing up these lengths:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Perimeter} = 6 + 7 + 9 = 22 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the Scale Factor:**\n\n   We need to find the length of the sides of a similar triangle with a perimeter of 110 cm. Let's denote the scale factor $k$ by which the sides of the similar triangle are scaled by dividing the perimeter of the similar triangle by the perimeter of the given triangle:\n   \\[\n   k = \\frac{110 \\text{ cm}}{22 \\text{ cm}} = 5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the Other Sides of the Other Triangle:**\n\n   The sides of the original triangle are the base and one of the sides of the other, or they can be identified by the upper section's representation lengths (6 cm, 7 cm, or 9 cm).\n\n   - Based on the 6 cm side length:\n     \\[\n     6 \\cdot 5 = 30 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - Based on the 7 cm side length:\n     \\[\n     7 \\cdot 5 = 35 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - Based on the 9 cm side length:\n     \\[\n     9 \\cdot 5 = 45 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Identify the Longest Side Length:**\n\n   Comparing the lengths of the sides we obtained:\n   - 30 cm\n   - 35 cm\n   - 45 cm\n\n   Since 45 cm represents the longest side, the calculated length is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{45 \\text{ cm}}\n   \\]",
